tion to add the proud boys to  the list  we need to change our approach with the  outcome of dismantling these groups  there are as many as 300 white  supremacist violence groups that exist  in canada that pose an existential  threat  to canadians we need to be seeing action  on those groups as well  but it was an important step today  abigail beeman global news  ottawa still ahead a destructive fire  hits homes outside of perth australia  an out of control bushfire keeps raging  in western australia  hundreds more people had to make a  last-minute dash to safety  fleeing their homes on the outskirts of  perth the city is back in lockdown after  the first case of covet 19  in months was detected there the fierce  fast-moving fire doubled in size  overnight  it's the biggest the city has seen in  years  11 000 hectares have burned and 71 homes  have been lost  many more are in danger as relentless  winds keep fanning the flames  in russia independent monitors of the  police estimate 10 thousand people have  been taken into custody  since opposition leader alexei navalny  was arrested  and after his prison sentence yesterday  riot police  cracked down again  demonstrations in moscow and saint  petersburg were beaten back  riot police appeared to grab protesters  without obvious provocation  throwing them into police vehicles  journalists have been arrested too  and human rights groups say some people  are unaccounted for  the kremlin calls the protests illegal  and unauthorized and accuses the west  of descending into hysteria over  navalny's imprisonment  he was sentenced to three and a half  years in a penal colony a case navalny  says was  fabricated and politically motivated  well after the military coup in myanmar  also known as burma  police have now charged the country's  elected civilian leader  aung san tsuchi has been charged with  possessing  illegally imported walkie-talkies it  gives military leaders a legal reason to  hold her  until at least the middle 